---
source: crates/fauxfield/tests/cli.rs
expression: out
---
Run the MCP server for agents (SPEC §11.1). Logs go to stderr; stdout is protocol-only

Usage: fauxfield mcp [OPTIONS] [PATH]
       fauxfield mcp <COMMAND>

Commands:
  scenario  Run a scenario file against a running dev-mcp app (exit 0 pass, 1 failed step, 2 unreachable)
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [PATH]  Workspace folder to serve tools over

Options:
  -q, --quiet                  Suppress informational output
      --no-color               Disable coloured output (also honoured: the NO_COLOR environment variable)
      --transport <TRANSPORT>  Transport: stdio, unix, pipe (Windows), both, or http (streamable HTTP on 127.0.0.1)
      --socket <PATH>          Unix socket path, or a pipe name on Windows (default: per-user runtime dir, mcp-<pid>.sock; \\\\.\\pipe\\fauxfield-mcp-<pid>)
      --host <ADDR>            Bind address for --transport http. Only loopback is accepted (default 127.0.0.1)
      --port <PORT>            Port for --transport http (default: a random free port). Binds 127.0.0.1 only
      --allow <CLASSES>        Tool classes to expose: read, write, execute (default: all)
      --read-only              Shorthand for --allow read
  -h, --help                   Print help
